    "summary": "FFmpeg versions 2.1 through 8.1.2 contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the VobSub...",
    "details": "FFmpeg versions 2.1 through 8.1.2 contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the VobSub subtitle demuxer that allows attackers to corrupt adjacent heap memory by supplying a malicious .sub/.idx subtitle file declaring more distinct stream IDs than the fixed-size array bounds in `libavformat/mpeg.c`. Attackers can craft a subtitle file with excessive distinct stream IDs to trigger unbounded writes beyond the vobsub->q[] array boundary via `ff_subtitles_queue_insert()`, potentially achieving arbitrary code execution in any application using FFmpeg's VobSub demuxer.",
    "severity": [
